    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "In ASCVD, start a statin @ the maximally tolerated dose aiming to lower LDL-C by > 50% (high-intensity). In very high-risk ASCVD (eg, recent MI or unstable angina, or diabetes), LDL-C > 70 mg/dL despite maximal statin should prompt adding ezetimibe or a PCSK9i."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "W TG < 500 mg/dL and a raised LDL-C, a statin can lower both; if only TG are ↑, fibrates are the drug of choice."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "MSD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " routine LFT monitoring isn't necessary, and routine CK doesn't predict rhabdomyolysis; check musc enzymes only if myalgias or other musc Sx develop. If Sx don't subside w.in 1 to 2 wks off the statin, look for another cause (eg, polymyalgia rheumatica)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Atorvastatin:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " use w cyclosporine or gemfibrozil = ⍉recommended; ⍉more than 1.2 L/day of grapefruit juice."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Atorvastatin:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " tell pts to promptly report unexplained musc pain, tenderness or weakness, esp w malaise or fever."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
